{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"decoder"},{"kind":"text","text":": any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Decoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decoding allocates a page table entry for every page of 1024 positions from the first listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position to the end, and a page for each page holding a listed element; positions before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first listed one cost nothing. An end is implausible when that span is more than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"16 × count + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pages, where "},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of vertices (or edges) listed: at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"16 page table entries per listed element (about 2 KB for a vertex, 256 bytes for an edge)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus 64. So "},{"code":"\"vertexEnd\": 4611686018427387903","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with no vertices decodes, in O(1), while a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"payload cannot make decoding allocate without limit. A graph that has run more than that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many empty pages past its live elements does not round-trip."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/StableGraphs\/documentation\/StableGraphs","doc:\/\/StableGraphs\/documentation\/StableGraphs\/StableDirectedGraph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":